[ENTRYPOINT] Error: this image ran 'init-build-env' (build mode) during its build.

Build mode is only meant for builder stages of a multi-stage build — an image like this
must not be booted: the boot would reset the build-time work data and silently discard
changes made by later build steps.

Fix: run your build in a builder stage and copy the artifacts into a fresh final stage:

    FROM neunerlei/php-nginx:latest AS builder
    RUN init-build-env
    RUN <your build commands>

    FROM neunerlei/php-nginx:latest
    COPY --from=builder /var/www/html ./

If you really need to boot such an image (e.g. to run tests in a CI builder stage),
build it with 'init-build-env --allow-boot' instead.

Documentation: https://github.com/Neunerlei/docker-images/blob/main/docs/common.md#build-mode
Migration guide: https://github.com/Neunerlei/docker-images/blob/main/docs/migration/2026-11-12-build-mode-marker-and-variables.md
